cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Copernicopia, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Copernicopia: Download Copernicus Marine Data and Append It to Your Own Data"
version: 1.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-12
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23901767
authors:
  - family-names: Viola
    given-names: Benjamin
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2620-2914"
    affiliation: "Institute for Marine and Antarctic Studies, University of Tasmania, Hobart, Australia; School of Biological Sciences, Monash University, Clayton, Australia"
    email: benjamin.viola@utas.edu.au
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/BMViola/copernicopia"
url: "https://github.com/BMViola/copernicopia"
abstract: >-
  An R package that guides users through downloading gridded data from the
  Copernicus Marine Service, using the official copernicusmarine Python toolbox,
  and appending the values to their own data by location, time and depth. It
  offers a step-by-step wizard or scripted requests, downloads that can be
  cancelled and resumed, regions that cross 180 degrees, and a record of the
  sources needed to cite the data. Its values have been validated against an
  independent extraction.
keywords:
  - R
  - Copernicus Marine Service
  - oceanography
  - marine ecology
  - satellite data
  - environmental data
